From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@t1100.local>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:00:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: add the ITE IT6112 / BOE TV110XUM-LB2 panel driver

Port the WIP driver from the mt6771-next tree (adomerle, 6.16,
refs/it6112/panel-it6112-boe-tv110xum-lb2.c in t1100-ubuntu, cited file
sha256 4d4dd33a...) to 6.12. The panel of the Fplus T1100 (BOE
TV110XUM-LB2, 1600x2176) is not on DSI0 directly: an ITE IT6112 bridge
sits between the host and the panel, converts the 4-lane DSI stream to
dual DSI and forwards DCS commands written to its register 0x73.

All register sequences, the I2C addresses (TX 0x56, RX dummy 0x5e) and
the mode timings are taken unchanged from that source, which itself
documents them as the reverse of the LK init.

Changes needed by 6.12 (and one real bug in the original):

 - devm_drm_panel_alloc() only exists since 6.16; use devm_kzalloc() +
   drm_panel_init().
 - mipi_dsi_device_match() falls back to comparing the DSI device name
   with the driver name (drivers/gpu/drm/drm_mipi_dsi.c:59). The original
   named the peripheral "boe-tv110xum-lb2" and the driver
   "panel-boe-tv110xum-lb2-it6112", so it could never bind; both use
   IT6112_DSI_NAME now.
 - probe powers DVDD/VPOS/VNEG around the product-id read instead of
   trusting the state LK left behind, so the bridge is detected even if
   the rails are off.
 - I2C write errors are reported (the original tested the register
   number instead of the return value, so every good write logged an
   error), masked reads no longer write back negative values, and the
   MCLK measurement cannot divide by zero any more when the bridge does
   not answer.
 - the DSI peripheral is unregistered and detached on remove, and the
   panel is only removed after that.

Not tested on hardware yet: the sequences are the reference ones, the
mode is 1600x2176@60 RGB888 on 4 lanes (1.535 Gbps/lane, which also
needs the mtk_dsi mode_valid fix that follows).
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig                 |  12 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile                |   1 +
 .../drm/panel/panel-it6112-boe-tv110xum-lb2.c | 606 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 619 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-it6112-boe-tv110xum-lb2.c

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
index 67fc67134..3464a5aa1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
@@ -401,6 +401,18 @@ config DRM_PANEL_INNOLUX_P079ZCA
 	  24 bit RGB per pixel. It provides a MIPI DSI interface to
 	  the host and has a built-in LED backlight.
 
+config DRM_PANEL_IT6112_BOE_TV110XUM_LB2
+	tristate "BOE TV110XUM-LB2 1600x2176 panel on an ITE IT6112 bridge"
+	depends on OF
+	depends on DRM_MIPI_DSI
+	depends on BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE
+	depends on I2C
+	help
+	  Say Y here if you want to enable support for the BOE TV110XUM-LB2
+	  panel as found in the Fplus T1100 tablet. The panel is driven through
+	  an ITE IT6112 DSI-to-dual-DSI bridge that is configured over I2C and
+	  forwards DCS commands to the panel.
+
 config DRM_PANEL_JADARD_JD9365DA_H3
 	tristate "Jadard JD9365DA-H3 WXGA DSI panel"
 	depends on OF
